ial_and_power_function_09a98329_003","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"The nonzero constant function $f(x)=7$ can be written as $7x^{0}$. As a monomial, what is its degree?","options":["$1$","undefined","$0$","$7$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ec092eee8e2ead8fcf82be58"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_monomial_and_power_function_09a98329_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which example is a power function with a singularity at $0$?","options":["$f(x) = x^{-1}$","$f(x) = 3x^2$","$f(x) = x$","$f(x) = 2x^3$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e3f5edcee244a93c89d0d07b"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_monomial_and_power_function_09a98329_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What roles do the coefficient and exponent play in $f(x) = a x^k$?","options":["The coefficient controls scaling, while the exponent controls growth behaviour","The coefficient controls the domain, while the exponent controls notation only","The coefficient is always the degree, while the exponent is always real-valued output","The coefficient controls singularity, while the exponent must be $1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e03d3f5ef11c022ddf123951"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_monomial_and_power_function_09a98329_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which statement best describes the relation between monomials and power functions in this context?","options":["A power function is allowed only when the exponent is natural, in every case without exception.","A monomial is the case where the exponent is natural; a power function allows a real exponent","A monomial must have exponent $-1$","A power function cannot have a coefficient"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"6d2964cfed92243dfe8c6511"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_monomial_and_power_function_09a98329_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"applicati